WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.002
- This is one of the
greatest play-action fakes

00:00:02.002 --> 00:00:03.211
I’ve ever seen in my entire life.
- [Sean McVay:] It was a good fake.

00:00:03.211 --> 00:00:04.963
Look at them: They were, they
were celebratin’ right here.

00:00:04.963 --> 00:00:05.547
- [Adam Lefkoe:] They all bit.

00:00:05.547 --> 00:00:06.965
- [McVay:] You see 'em? Look at this.
- [Lefkoe:] Oh yeah, they're jumpin' into each other!

00:00:06.965 --> 00:00:08.967
- [McVay:] They think they made the play.

00:00:08.967 --> 00:00:11.219
This is "Fake 32 Wham Naked Left."

00:00:11.219 --> 00:00:13.179
- [Lefkoe laughing]

00:00:13.221 --> 00:00:16.307
- Yo! Lefkoe out here in L.A.
to meet with maybe the

00:00:16.307 --> 00:00:18.601
smartest coach in the NFL,
Sean McVay,

00:00:18.601 --> 00:00:22.856
a brain so big, he remembers
every play he’s ever called.

00:00:22.856 --> 00:00:25.233
I remember every call
I’ve had with my

00:00:25.233 --> 00:00:27.694
State Farm agent, talking
auto and home insurance.

00:00:27.736 --> 00:00:31.406
Paul! The calls we’ve had! Amazing!

00:00:31.406 --> 00:00:32.490
Enough about that.

00:00:32.490 --> 00:00:34.868
Let’s go Ditch the Playbook with Sean McVay.

00:00:34.868 --> 00:00:37.746
♪♪♪

00:00:44.252 --> 00:00:45.295
Sean McVay.

00:00:45.879 --> 00:00:46.504
How are you, man?

00:00:46.504 --> 00:00:47.756
- Good to see ya, man.
- Good to see you too.

00:00:47.756 --> 00:00:49.924
- All right.
- Dude, you’re the man, dude.

00:00:49.924 --> 00:00:50.425
- Yeah, right.

00:00:50.425 --> 00:00:51.176
- Get over here.

00:00:51.176 --> 00:00:56.181
Last year, we stood here, and I didn’t
realize we were gonna set the internet ablaze.

00:00:56.181 --> 00:00:57.015
- (Laughing)

00:00:57.015 --> 00:01:00.268
- I’m sure you got sent that clip a million times–
- Yeah, it was fun.
- of you remembering everything.

00:01:00.477 --> 00:01:03.104
Fifty eight seconds left
in the fourth quarter.

00:01:03.104 --> 00:01:05.023
- Jamison Crowder wheel
route on the right sideline.

00:01:05.356 --> 00:01:07.358
I don’t remember anything
except for that stuff.

00:01:07.358 --> 00:01:08.276
- Except for football?
- Yeah, exactly.

00:01:08.276 --> 00:01:12.155
- I was wondering, is your fiancee ever
like, “You forgot the groceries today.”

00:01:12.155 --> 00:01:16.076
- Oh, yeah, she’s like, “You’re a total vegetable
in life except for when it comes to football.”

00:01:16.076 --> 00:01:17.202
So, no doubt about it.

00:01:17.202 --> 00:01:19.788
- So, if Sean McVay forgets
things, we’re all screwed.

00:01:19.788 --> 00:01:20.872
So we’re all safe.
- (Laughing)

00:01:20.872 --> 00:01:24.417
- We know that you can
remember every play you ever called.

00:01:24.417 --> 00:01:25.710
- I don’t know about that.

00:01:25.710 --> 00:01:28.922
- But: Do you remember the
plays in which you played?

00:01:29.506 --> 00:01:30.340
We’re gonna take you on a journey—

00:01:30.340 --> 00:01:31.966
- Try to get those memories out of my mind.

00:01:31.966 --> 00:01:33.218
- No, no, no!

00:01:33.218 --> 00:01:36.012
Cuz this is “Mr. Georgia Football.”

00:01:36.012 --> 00:01:37.931
Do you know what’s gonna happen in this play?

00:01:38.098 --> 00:01:41.476
- (McVay) That’s, uh, it’s gonna be a
touchdown pass down the right sideline right here.

00:01:41.476 --> 00:01:42.560
- Oh, my gosh.

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:44.395
Let’s watch this in all of its glory.

00:01:44.395 --> 00:01:44.938
Do you remember the—

00:01:44.938 --> 00:01:45.939
- I get drilled right here.

00:01:45.939 --> 00:01:46.981
- You do on the sideline.

00:01:46.981 --> 00:01:48.149
- “876 Trail Flood.”

00:01:48.691 --> 00:01:49.984
- That’s incredible.

00:01:49.984 --> 00:01:50.902
- Yeah, I mean, but that’s a—

00:01:50.902 --> 00:01:53.571
- In the Georgia Dome—50-yard touchdown bomb.

00:01:53.571 --> 00:01:56.116
- I just heaved it up as far as
I could and then got drilled.

00:01:56.116 --> 00:01:58.660
And then I heard the cheers and
just was hoping it wasn’t a pick.

00:01:58.660 --> 00:01:59.786
- So you didn’t even see it.

00:01:59.786 --> 00:02:00.787
- No.
- You’re just on the sideline.

00:02:00.787 --> 00:02:02.622
- I didn’t see it.
My freaking helmet.

00:02:02.622 --> 00:02:05.625
I was in the, I was in the freaking
stands right there, it felt like.

00:02:05.625 --> 00:02:06.376
- All right.

00:02:06.376 --> 00:02:07.210
- Good catch.

00:02:07.210 --> 00:02:08.670
- I got another one for ya.

00:02:08.670 --> 00:02:10.171
You weren’t just a thrower.

00:02:10.171 --> 00:02:12.757
- I was more of a runner.
- My man McVay had wheels.

00:02:12.757 --> 00:02:13.842
So this run.

00:02:15.593 --> 00:02:16.469
Look at that juke.

00:02:16.469 --> 00:02:18.638
- You can’t show me gettin’ hawked, though.

00:02:18.638 --> 00:02:19.597
I don’t finish it.

00:02:19.597 --> 00:02:21.558
I get tackled at the 2 right here.

00:02:21.558 --> 00:02:25.478
I got killed from, for this one by my
buddies, that I got tackled right here.

00:02:25.478 --> 00:02:27.313
- (Laughing)
- I still haven’t lived that one down.

00:02:27.313 --> 00:02:30.817
My buddies, they say, “Hey, how’s this guy
from Tucker doin’ that hawked you down?”

00:02:31.985 --> 00:02:33.361
- They still talk to you about this run?

00:02:33.361 --> 00:02:36.698
- Oh, man, of course. I get ragged on by my buddies.
- This is a 78-yard run.

00:02:36.698 --> 00:02:38.324
- Shoulda been 80.

00:02:38.324 --> 00:02:41.286
- You also apparently were calling
your own plays in high school?

00:02:41.286 --> 00:02:43.204
- (Laughing)
- Let’s bring it up.

00:02:43.204 --> 00:02:43.788
- Yeah.

00:02:43.788 --> 00:02:45.748
- This is one of the
greatest play-action fakes

00:02:45.748 --> 00:02:46.833
I’ve ever seen in my entire life.
- It was a good fake.

00:02:46.833 --> 00:02:48.793
Look at them: They were, they
were celebratin’ right there.

00:02:48.793 --> 00:02:49.294
- They all bit.

00:02:49.294 --> 00:02:50.712
- See ‘em there?
They’re celebratin’.

00:02:50.712 --> 00:02:51.754
- Hold on. Let me watch that again.

00:02:51.754 --> 00:02:53.381
- Watch these guys on the defense.

00:02:53.381 --> 00:02:55.884
They get up. I’m glad the
ref didn’t blow it dead.

00:02:55.884 --> 00:02:57.802
Watch ‘em. They’re celebrating like—
- Oh, yeah.

00:02:57.802 --> 00:03:00.471
They’re jumpin’ into each other.
- They think they made the play.

00:03:00.471 --> 00:03:03.474
- (Lefkoe) Now I heard
that you called this play?

00:03:03.474 --> 00:03:05.059
Or you diagrammed this?

00:03:05.059 --> 00:03:05.935
What was the name of it.

00:03:05.935 --> 00:03:09.063
- This is, this is “Fake 32 Wham Naked Left.”

00:03:09.063 --> 00:03:10.356
- (Laughing)

00:03:10.356 --> 00:03:13.943
- So this was, this was
one of the best defenses in the state.

00:03:13.943 --> 00:03:16.487
They were really tough
to, to get the ball in.

00:03:16.487 --> 00:03:17.780
And you know, we’re inside the 5.

00:03:17.780 --> 00:03:18.907
This was third down.

00:03:18.907 --> 00:03:22.785
I say, “Hey, they way they’re pursuin’, I
think the “32 Wham Naked” would work.” And,

00:03:22.785 --> 00:03:27.040
they, you know, we all agreed, and fortunately
I didn’t get drilled in the back of the head.

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:29.417
And we walked in, and we ended
up winnin’ this game right here.

00:03:29.417 --> 00:03:32.962
- When I see a quarterback willing to
completely turn his back to the defense—

00:03:32.962 --> 00:03:33.463
- It’s a leap of faith.

00:03:33.463 --> 00:03:34.464
- You, you sold it.

00:03:34.464 --> 00:03:35.423
And this was the playoffs, right?

00:03:35.423 --> 00:03:37.550
- This is, this is good
ball-handling right there—hiding it.

00:03:37.550 --> 00:03:38.468
Good ball-handling.

00:03:38.468 --> 00:03:41.346
That’s the only thing I could do—the
things that really take no talent.

00:03:41.346 --> 00:03:42.639
(Laughing)
- You need to show this to Jared.

00:03:42.639 --> 00:03:44.599
This is how he needs to
sell play action this year.

00:03:45.308 --> 00:03:46.893
- That—now I can’t even look at that.

00:03:46.893 --> 00:03:48.269
Look at that bowl cut, man.

00:03:48.269 --> 00:03:51.189
You look like you just put a bowl right
over my head and just cut right around it.

00:03:51.189 --> 00:03:54.567
- This is every Georgia high school
athlete for, like, the last two decades.

00:03:54.567 --> 00:03:55.193
- It’s horrible.

00:03:55.652 --> 00:03:58.696
I look like I’m from, uh,
the one MTV show—Hoover High.

00:03:58.696 --> 00:03:59.864
- Yes, exactly!

00:03:59.864 --> 00:04:01.241
Hoover High—that’s what I’m thinking.

00:04:01.241 --> 00:04:02.033
- (McVay) Exactly.

00:04:02.033 --> 00:04:06.579
- I know how you played football, so I believe
that there was one movie that I think—

00:04:06.579 --> 00:04:08.831
- (Laughing)
- and there was one character
that really spoke to you.

00:04:08.831 --> 00:04:10.375
(Drum roll)
- Varsity Blues?
- Yes.

00:04:10.375 --> 00:04:11.834
- Oh, yeah.
- I believe—

00:04:11.834 --> 00:04:12.835
- Don’t compare me to Tweeder.

00:04:12.835 --> 00:04:14.837
- I think that you were a Tweeder guy.

00:04:14.837 --> 00:04:16.881
- (Laughing)
Nah, I don’t know if I was really anyone.

00:04:16.881 --> 00:04:18.049
I was pretty serious then.

00:04:18.049 --> 00:04:19.592
You know, Tweeder had more fun.

00:04:19.592 --> 00:04:22.804
I wish I was like Tweeder in high school
where I enjoyed myself a little bit more.

00:04:22.804 --> 00:04:24.389
I probably was too serious in high school.

00:04:24.389 --> 00:04:30.061
- But what I want to do is break down the
realistic—if these plays could ever be used.

00:04:30.103 --> 00:04:32.730
Billy Bob snaps, lays a nice block.

00:04:32.730 --> 00:04:35.942
Tweeder—I don’t know what
defense that corner was playing.

00:04:35.942 --> 00:04:38.403
- This guy’s playing jam with no backup.

00:04:38.403 --> 00:04:39.946
- And we got Billy Bob out there.

00:04:39.946 --> 00:04:41.072
Tweeder’s gonna catch it.

00:04:41.072 --> 00:04:42.240
I mean, do you remember this, like?

00:04:42.240 --> 00:04:42.699
- Oh, yeah.

00:04:42.699 --> 00:04:44.367
Double stop sign right there.

00:04:44.367 --> 00:04:46.911
That’s how you know Tweeder
wasn’t really playin’ receiver.

00:04:46.911 --> 00:04:48.162
The “Hook and Ladder”?

00:04:48.162 --> 00:04:50.123
- Who on the Rams is the most Billy Bob?

00:04:50.832 --> 00:04:53.001
I think it’s that fourth-round
draft pick you guys just got.

00:04:53.001 --> 00:04:54.335
The defensive line—
- Greg Gaines?

00:04:54.335 --> 00:04:55.670
- Greg Gaines is a little Billy Bob.

00:04:55.670 --> 00:04:58.131
- Greg Gaines is Billy Bob right now.

00:04:58.131 --> 00:04:59.716
That’s exactly right.
- I saw him on the practice field, and I was—

00:04:59.716 --> 00:05:01.259
- I’d like to see, he looks really,
you know, runnin’ with the ball—

00:05:01.259 --> 00:05:03.011
I can see Big Greg Gaines.

00:05:03.011 --> 00:05:04.345
- Right? It’s perfect.

00:05:04.345 --> 00:05:06.806
- That’s pretty good right there.
- All right. I got another one for ya.

00:05:06.806 --> 00:05:08.558
Uh, don’t get angry at me.

00:05:08.558 --> 00:05:09.642
- Freaking predictable.

00:05:09.642 --> 00:05:12.437
- So let me ask you: Was Rudy offsides?

00:05:13.479 --> 00:05:14.772
- Absolutely.
- Let’s take a look.

00:05:14.772 --> 00:05:15.898
Absolutely?

00:05:15.898 --> 00:05:17.150
All right, so he lines up.

00:05:17.150 --> 00:05:18.568
He has no idea where to go.

00:05:19.319 --> 00:05:21.696
Aww, the janitor was so intense.

00:05:22.780 --> 00:05:24.407
I mean, this had to juice
you up a little bit though?

00:05:25.950 --> 00:05:27.076
- Nope.

00:05:27.076 --> 00:05:28.745
I’m kidding.
I’m being hard on ol’ Rudy.

00:05:28.745 --> 00:05:31.289
- So, right there, you think
he’s offsides right there?

00:05:31.289 --> 00:05:32.874
- It’s called an elite get-off, man.

00:05:32.874 --> 00:05:34.709
He’s keying the ball right there.

00:05:34.709 --> 00:05:35.877
He doesn’t get blocked.

00:05:35.877 --> 00:05:37.503
He finds a way to finish the play.

00:05:37.503 --> 00:05:40.048
Man, great play by “Ruuudy!”

00:05:40.048 --> 00:05:41.090
- Ruuudy!

00:05:41.090 --> 00:05:42.425
Ruuu— Damn.

00:05:42.425 --> 00:05:43.468
Small white guys, man.

00:05:43.468 --> 00:05:44.177
It’s tough.

00:05:44.177 --> 00:05:45.428
- (Laughing)
- It all goes back to that.

00:05:45.428 --> 00:05:48.348
The last play that I really
want to get involved, though is—

00:05:48.723 --> 00:05:49.807
- (McVay) Little Giants?

00:05:49.807 --> 00:05:50.433
- Yes.

00:05:51.517 --> 00:05:54.604
- Little Giants is a, I love Little Giants.

00:05:54.604 --> 00:05:57.774
- I think that you’re—every team
is looking for their Icebox, right?

00:05:57.774 --> 00:05:59.108
But do you remember the name of this play?

00:05:59.817 --> 00:06:01.486
- “Annexation of Puerto Rico”?

00:06:01.486 --> 00:06:03.071
- That’s my man right there.
- There ya go, man.

00:06:03.071 --> 00:06:06.240
- Annexation of Puerto Rico:
They give the ball to Icebox.

00:06:06.240 --> 00:06:07.408
It’s the old “Fumblerooski.”

00:06:07.408 --> 00:06:08.951
- It really is. It’s a great play.

00:06:08.951 --> 00:06:10.953
- Can we bring the “Fumblerooski” back?

00:06:10.953 --> 00:06:12.080
I don’t even know if that’s legal.

00:06:12.080 --> 00:06:13.247
- I don’t either, honestly.

00:06:13.247 --> 00:06:17.251
You know, we change these rules so
often, I gotta refer to somebody else.

00:06:17.251 --> 00:06:19.545
You know, we got coaches
that’re way better experts.

00:06:19.545 --> 00:06:22.090
I, I, sometimes I don’t even
know what a rule is anymore.

00:06:22.090 --> 00:06:24.467
- What, what we’re ruling on things anymore.
- Yeah. We don’t know what a catch is.

00:06:24.467 --> 00:06:26.386
We don’t know what pass
interference— Sorry.

00:06:27.220 --> 00:06:27.887
- Worked in our favor.

00:06:27.887 --> 00:06:28.513
- Yeah, right?

00:06:28.513 --> 00:06:29.305
It was awesome.

00:06:29.305 --> 00:06:30.014
- Hey.

00:06:30.014 --> 00:06:32.392
- Thank you for taking this journey with me.
- Yeah, it was fun.

00:06:32.392 --> 00:06:33.476
- (Lefkoe) I really appreciate it.
- Yeah.

00:06:33.476 --> 00:06:35.645
- Sean McVay—ditchin’ the playbook.

00:06:35.645 --> 00:06:37.647
I love you, man. Thanks for doin’ this.
- Good to see you, man.

00:06:37.647 --> 00:06:39.399
- Thanks for being such a good sport.
- That was fun, man.

00:06:41.401 --> 00:06:44.237
- What's up, y'all. This is Mohamed Sanu
with the Atlanta Falcons.

00:06:44.237 --> 00:06:48.491
Make sure y'all subscribe to Bleacher Report
YouTube for more videos like this.

